  "scoring_key_verified": true,
  "notes": "Brief 14-item form = CRS items 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 16, 20, 22, 24, 25, 27, 33, 34 (Feinberg, Brown & Kan 2012, verified from source_url), listed here in ascending CRS order with each item's crs_item recorded: endorsement {1, 4}, closeness {2, 24}, division of labor {5, 20}, agreement {6, 9}, undermining {16, 22}, support {25, 27}, exposure to conflict {33, 34}. Scale 0 = not true of us … 6 = very true of us (CRS 1–30); exposure items 31–35 use 0 = never … 6 = very often. Reverse-keyed within their subscales: CRS 9 (agreement) and CRS 20 (division of labor); undermining and exposure items are scored so that higher = more of that construct (the article reverses them only when forming a positive-coparenting total). Subscales are means. Undermining or exposure above the midpoint (3) triggers a weight-3 parenting flag. The administration order of the brief form should be confirmed against the official form when transcribing text.",
  "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3499623/",
  "text_source": "Item text not populated (journal copyright; obtain the measure from Feinberg's group at Penn State's Prevention Research Center or the article appendix). Scoring key verified from the open-access article."
